Falcon 4K

Falcon is derived from Sonic firmware by Robby (Robby69400) and contributors,
and incorporates work from Armel F4HWN, Dual Tachyon, egzumer and nToivola.
The CHIRP driver derives from the work of Jacek Lipkowski, EGZUMER, JOC2,
Dan Smith and F4HWN; see its copyright and GPL license notices.
Third-party drivers and libraries retain their original notices.
This is not an official release from the upstream Sonic or F4HWN projects.

Overlay loader, selector and configuration-proxy API services
are derived from Armel F4HWN v6.2.0, commit
0ade03c0b1c94514566fadf7ce1c7a1f542a2283 (Apache-2.0).
Falcon-specific modules use the same RAM workspace and retain BIN CRC binding.

Overlay API level 3 services and the 40 official application packages and
sources follow F4HWN v6.3.0, commit
ca3a4271386049e7b459b215cef0ad0eea1a30ca (Apache-2.0).
Falcon adapts wire-format step and power IDs to its own unchanged memory layout.

The stack watermark (stack_usage.c) and the external asset-zone location
follow F4HWN v7 (branch feature_update_v7, Apache-2.0).
